import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MachineLearning_TransformerUniversality_ContinuousUniversality

/-!
# Genuine continuous universality on compact sequence domains

`Catalog/MachineLearning/TransformerArchitecture.lean` proves *exact* universality on a finite
domain, and `FiniteLookupSeparation.lean` shows that a quantized finite lookup table can never
be a continuous universal approximator (its uniform error against the identity on `[0,1]` is
at least `1/(2N)`).  This file supplies the missing genuine continuous statement.

The architecture considered here is the closure of the linear-attention *readouts*
`x ↦ ∑ i a, w i a * x i a` under sums and products; products model multiplicative
(gated / feed-forward) mixing layers, and the whole class is the `ℝ`-subalgebra
`attentionAlgebra` of `C(X, ℝ)` generated by the readouts.

Main results:

* `attentionAlgebra_separatesPoints` — readouts already separate sequences;
* `attention_uniform_universal` — **uniform universal approximation**: every continuous
  real-valued functional of a sequence is uniformly `ε`-approximated on every compact set of
  sequences by an element of `attentionAlgebra`;
* `attention_seq2seq_uniform_universal` — the sequence-to-sequence version, uniform in all
  output positions and features simultaneously.

Taken with the separation theorem, this delimits the situation exactly: exact finite lookup is
*not* the continuous theorem, and the continuous theorem needs the multiplicative structure,
not just attention selection.
-/

open scoped BigOperators

open ContinuousUniversality

variable {ι κ : Type*} [Fintype ι] [Fintype κ]










open ContinuousUniversality in
theorem solution[DecidableEq ι] [DecidableEq κ] (i₀ : ι) (a₀ : κ) (x : Seq ι κ) :
    readoutCM (fun i a => if i = i₀ ∧ a = a₀ then (1:ℝ) else 0) x = x i₀ a₀ := by
  show ∑ i, ∑ a, (if i = i₀ ∧ a = a₀ then (1:ℝ) else 0) * x i a = x i₀ a₀
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single i₀]
  · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single a₀]
    · simp
    · intro a _ ha; simp [ha]
    · intro h; exact absurd (Finset.mem_univ a₀) h
  · intro i _ hi
    apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
    intro a _
    simp [hi]
  · intro h; exact absurd (Finset.mem_univ i₀) h
